      },
      "text": [
        " عَلَى الْإِمَامِ أَنْ يُصَلِّيَ الظُّهْرَ بِمِنًى ثُمَّ يَبِيتُ بِهَا وَ يُصْبِحُ حَتَّى تَطْلُعَ الشَّمْسُ ثُمَّ يَخْرُجُ إِلَى عَرَفَاتٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Jameel Bin Darraj, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘It is upon the Prayer-leader that he Prays Al-Zohr at Mina, then he sleeps over till the sun emerges, then he goes out to Arafaat’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Jamil ibn Darraj who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘An Imam must perform Salat (prayer) of al-Zuhr in Mina 5 , stay the night there till the morning until sunrise; then leave for ‘Arafat . ‘“ "
        ]
      }
    },
